@startuml tommy-workflow
' Tommy — Spec-Driven Development workflow: possible flows, conditionals, and observations.
title Tommy — Spec-Driven Development Workflow

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F0F4FF
  BorderColor #4A6FA5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

|Bootstrap|
start
if (.tommy/ scaffolding complete?\nscripts + templates + project-context + codebase, all present) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Tommy Start\n(scaffold .tommy/, research codebase\n& product context, fill TOMMY.md,\ncreate AGENTS.md);
  note right
    Every Tommy agent self-checks for this
    scaffolding and self-triggers Tommy Start
    if it is missing — the workflow never
    hard-fails just because /tommy-start
    was skipped.
  end note
endif

|Specify|
:Describe the feature in natural language;
:Create feature branch "NNN-short-name" and spec.md;
:Business Analyst elicits requirements\n(targeted questions, 3-5 at a time);
repeat
  :Write / refine spec.md\n(goals, user stories, acceptance criteria, non-goals);
repeat while (Passes the spec quality checklist?) is (no — fix and retry, up to 3x) not (yes)
note right
  If still failing after 3 iterations, escalate
  the open questions to the user instead of
  looping forever.
end note

|Prompt|
:Reference the approved spec;
:Architect designs implementation architecture,\nbounded contexts, data model;
:Write detailed implementation plan + its own checklist;
:Plan file ready in .tommy/specs/.../plans/;

|Codegen|
:Pick one plan file to implement;
if (Plan's own checklist fully checked?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Stop and report the plan\nas not yet validated;
  stop
endif
repeat
  :Implement / fix code and tests;
repeat while (Quality gate passes?\nlint, tests, complexity, pattern\ncompliance, Sonar, checklist) is (no) not (yes)
:Code ready — report to user;

|Versioning|
note right
  Not a fourth phase — two independent
  actions available at any point, each only
  ever triggered by an EXPLICIT user request.
  No Tommy agent commits or opens a PR/MR
  on its own initiative.
end note

fork
  if (User explicitly asks to commit?) then (yes)
    :Tommy Commit — review diff,\npropose Conventional Commit message(s);
    if (User confirms message & files?) then (yes)
      :git commit\n(one or more commits per branch/plan,\ne.g. one per finished checklist item);
    else (no)
      :Revise the proposed message;
    endif
  else (not yet)
  endif
fork again
  if (User explicitly asks to open a PR/MR?) then (yes)
    if (Provider already known in\n.tommy/codebase/integrations.md?) then (yes)
    else (no)
      if (Remote hostname matches a known pattern —\ngithub.com, gitlab*, dev.azure.com or visualstudio.com?) then (yes)
      else (no)
        :Ask the user which\nprovider/tool to use;
        note right
          Self-hosted hostnames are not
          reliable evidence — never guess.
          The answer is recorded in
          integrations.md so this is not
          asked again next time.
        end note
      endif
    endif
    switch (Detected provider?)
    case ( GitHub )
      :gh pr create;
    case ( GitLab )
      :glab mr create;
      note right: GitLab calls this a\nMerge Request, not a Pull Request.
    case ( Azure DevOps )
      :az repos pr create;
    case ( Unsupported host — e.g. GCP\nCloud Source Repositories )
      :Push the branch only,\nreport that PR/MR is not\nsupported for this host;
    endswitch
    :Report the PR/MR URL to the user;
  else (not yet)
  endif
end fork

note right
  Never adds a "Co-authored-by:" trailer or any
  AI-attribution footer to a commit or PR/MR body.
  Commit author is always the local git identity
  (git config user.name / user.email).
end note

stop

legend right
  | Note | Meaning |
  | Claude Code | Full flow above: 5 dedicated agents\n(Specify, Business Analyst, Architect,\nPrompt, Codegen) + tommy-git with 4 skills\n(Conventional Commits + one adapter per provider). |
  | Cursor / GitHub Copilot | Same flow, condensed: Specify absorbs\nBusiness Analyst, Prompt absorbs Architect;\nCommit/Open-PR condensed into 2 files instead\nof 1 agent + 4 skills. Phase separation is\nself-enforced discipline, not tool-restricted. |
endlegend

@enduml
